From: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 04:54:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: preserve LAG output device in path walk

The flowtable path walker already passes immutable post-NAT flow keys to
fill_forward_path, allowing bonding to select the same slave as the
transmit path. Once bonding exposes that slave, the resulting path also
contains a DEV_PATH_LAG entry.

Handle that entry as an Ethernet-like path step and preserve the LAG
master as the software output device. Later path entries can then resolve
the selected lower device used for hardware redirection without replacing
the flow's software output interface.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6
Signed-off-by: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
@@ -151,12 +151,17 @@ static void nft_dev_path_info(const struct net_device_path_stack *stack,
 		case DEV_PATH_ETHERNET:
 		case DEV_PATH_DSA:
 		case DEV_PATH_VLAN:
+		case DEV_PATH_LAG:
 		case DEV_PATH_PPPOE:
 			if (is_zero_ether_addr(info->h_source))
 				memcpy(info->h_source, path->dev->dev_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 
 			if (path->type == DEV_PATH_ETHERNET)
 				break;
+			if (path->type == DEV_PATH_LAG) {
+				info->outdev = path->dev;
+				break;
+			}
 			if (path->type == DEV_PATH_DSA) {
 				i = stack->num_paths;
 				break;
